+//
+//  - the luma, per luma sample: the polynomial mapping (5.4.2.3.2) of the
+//    code s, read from a table made on the CPU with the clause's arithmetic,
+//    plus the inverse-quantized residual (5.4.3.2), also from a table;
+//  - the chroma, per chroma sample: the luma down-sampled as 5.4.2.3.3 says
+//    ([1 2 1] across three columns of two rows, integer rounding), then each
+//    component mapped by its MMR piece (evaluated exactly, see dovi_ccm.c) or
+//    its polynomial piece (table), plus its residual;
+//  - the enhancement layer, when it is smaller than the base layer, resampled
+//    first as annex B.3 does (informative; resampling is not normative, clause
+//    4 note 1): a vertical pass, then a horizontal one, integer filters,
+//    edges by replication of the picture's samples.
